    "body": "This doesn't really make sense. You're still generating a wrapper function around some other function, but instead this time the \"function\" is some series of steps. I think you can eliminate all of this and just say \"Set _value_ to a function that performs the same series of steps as the IDL operation _P_ on object _O_\" or similar.\n",
